From 47e5099b1dd2cbfb56be5a45a1da196cf6c20973 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:08:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep staged background rows intact when the window is
 replaced

A whole-window upload reads each row into the tile ring's memory and frees
the ring's slots. When the VRAM cells already hold another window, as on
Continue (the map load uploaded the arrival's window first), each cell's
leaving tile was copied back into the first free slot, over the staged
row, before that row reached VRAM. Tiles came up with parts of other tiles:
shifted bands of ground around the tamer until the screen was entered again.

Skip the copy-back while a row is staged; the row read replaces the ring
anyway.
---
 src/main/tfs_stream.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main/tfs_stream.c b/src/main/tfs_stream.c
index ffb63e1..74c0cf1 100644
--- a/src/main/tfs_stream.c
+++ b/src/main/tfs_stream.c
@@ -803,6 +803,15 @@ static void captureOutgoing(RECT *rect, int32_t incoming)
 	}
 	old = TFS_CELL[c];
 	TFS_CELL[c] = incoming;
+	/*
+	 * A staged row (tfsStageRow) occupies the ring's memory and has freed its
+	 * slots: a capture now would write the leaving tile over the row's pixels
+	 * before they are uploaded (Continue replaces the window the map load
+	 * uploaded, so every cell has a tile leaving).
+	 */
+	if (TFS_SPAN_FIRST >= 0) {
+		return;
+	}
 	if (!TFS_ACTIVE || (old < 0) || (old == incoming) || (MOD_TFS_TILE_SEQ[old] < 0) ||
 	    (findSlot(old) >= 0)) {
 		return;
-- 
